title: 'cumulus: fix V3 scheduling parent picking'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    The V3 scheduling parent is found by walking back from the relay chain best
    block until a slot older than the one being produced for. That walk read the
    wall clock a second time to decide which slot that was. The slot timer wakes
    2ms before the slot it reports begins, on purpose, so a clock read at that
    moment still returns the previous slot and the walk stepped one block too far
    back, anchoring the candidate at an older relay block than intended. The slot
    timer's production slot is now threaded through and used as the single source
    of truth for the walk.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: minor
